Z||000000||BAM-BAM||04-21-2000||12:55 AM||||  How important is it to change, and where might I get a steering damper? I am rebuilding my front end on my 85GT and that is the one thing I have overlooked. Is it a necessary replacement? how long do they usualy last? I need just a little help. TIA for any info.<P> Thanx, BAM-BAM  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||04-21-2000||01:14 AM||||The Fiero Store sells a Monroe steering damper. It seem a little better than stock. Don't know if wrenchhead or carparts carries these. If they did they might be a few pennies cheaper. I got mine at F.S.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fieroshop||04-21-2000||01:20 AM||||The steering damper that I carry is a monroe and I sell it for less the the Fiero Store. Check it out at <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop,net" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroshop,net</A>  and go to online catalog.||||reg||1
Z||000003||lennyb4||04-21-2000||11:08 AM||||Hey FIEROSHOP....(or anyone trying to link to his site). If you look close at the link you'll notice there is a comma instead of a period towards the end of the link. Just though i would say something in case someone was trying to link through. Just chance the comma to a period and you'll go right there.||||reg||11
Z||000004||88 Fiero||04-21-2000||12:41 PM||||hmmmm...I took out my steering damper on my '85 SE and it's alot easier to steer without it...even tho' I was running 16 inch wheels...I dont really think you need it... On my '88..you dont even have this one on..||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||04-21-2000||12:52 PM||||my damper came off the day i bought the car... BlackGTs came off right after i noticed he still had one... both cars are 86s. The damper is just weight as far as i was concerned.. but it does help if your driving long highway trips. The expansion joins on bridges will pull the steering wheel... not enought to cause an accident but enought to notice. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||04-21-2000||02:11 PM||||You can get it anyplace. Wrenchead.com and carparts.com both have it.<P>It's partly a matter of preferance. can help allot if you drive in allot of rough stuff or hit a big puddle with only one front wheel.||||reg||1
Z||000007||DXR_DAD||04-21-2000||11:46 PM||||BAM-BAM, I replaced mine and got a Monroe from Kargen Auto Parts for $36.00<BR>Part # 7633910 and thats with Kargen's Lifetime Warranty. Just pulled my receipt book out to check price, didn't think I paid as much as the Fiero Store but I wanted to be sure.||||reg||1
